{"name":"Autumn’s Hill","hex":"#ba7a61","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"autumn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Traditionally the third of the four seasons, when deciduous trees lose their leaves, and temperatures and daylight hours decrease; typically regarded as spanning the months of September, October, and November in the Northern Hemisphere, and the months of March, April and May in the Southern Hemisphere.","The time period when someone or something is past its prime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the autumn (in a particular place).","To (cause to) undergo the changes associated with autumn, such as leaves changing color and falling from trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn"},{"term":"hill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevated landmass smaller than a mountain.","A sloping part of a landscape, especially one with a road, trail, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form into a heap or mound.","To heap or draw earth around plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill","wikidata":"Q54050"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn","wikidata":"Q1314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puijo Hill in Kuopio, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/500px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/1280px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/500px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate Hills of the Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/%D8%AA%D9%84_%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%88%D8%A7_%282%29.jpg/500px-%D8%AA%D9%84_%D8%B9%D9